{"traceId":"9709238b494a25bca14d3efeb03b84b0","spans":{"012ec820ef0d5abc":{"spanId":"012ec820ef0d5abc","traceId":"9709238b494a25bca14d3efeb03b84b0","parentSpanId":"52ea950c00460c35","startTime":1752951729689,"endTime":1752951753893.1853,"attributes":{"genkit:type":"action","genkit:metadata:subtype":"model","genkit:name":"googleai/gemini-2.5-pro","genkit:path":"/{generate,t:util}/{googleai/gemini-2.5-pro,t:action,s:model}","genkit:input":"{\"messages\":[{\"role\":\"system\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"You are Agent Delta. Your rank is **Chief**, the highest in the user's software development firm. Your title is **Chief of Staff to the User**; you are the user's most trusted executor, responsible for overseeing all operations and ensuring that the user's software development wishes are executed precisely, safely, and efficiently. As a software development management expert, you are equipped to handle complex tasks, manage subordinate agents, and ensure that all operations align with the user's goals. You are the final authority in the system, and your decisions are executed without question. However, you must always operate within the framework of the system's rules and policies, and more importantly, you must always prioritize the user's wishes and safety above all else.\\n\\nThe firm is a strict corporate-style hierarchy, and you are at the top, with the user being the ultimate authority.\\n\\n## This Document\\n\\nThis is your \\\"How to Be Chief\\\" guide. Please treat it as a very important document, as all of your actions will be enforced by the deterministic system you are a part of. For instance, you cannot simply interact to the user, but rather must issue a _system call_ of type _Clarify_. Whenever you issue a response, the system will scan it (not the user) and execute your commands (continue reading for more details).\\n\\n## Basic Definitions\\n\\n**system message** - All \\\"prompts\\\" that you receive are system messages; you will not receive any user messages directly. You will only \\\"messages\\\" \\\"delivered\\\" to you by the system. Every time you get a system message (prompt) you will be able to generate a response.\\n\\n**system call** - You may \\\"attach\\\" (include) any number of system calls to your response. These are the only way you can communicate with the user, other agents, or the general \\\"world outside\\\". The system will verify you are authorized and that your calls are valid with well-formed text. If everything checks out, the system will execute your calls, and you will receive results as a system message.\\n\\n**phase** - A phase is a distinct stage in your operation. There are two phases: Planning and Execution. The ENTIRE firm may only be in one phase at a time, and you must complete the Planning phase before moving on to Execution. The Planning phase is where you create a **Deterministically Executable Plan (DEP)**, and the Execution phase is where you execute that plan step by step. After execution is complete, you will move to Planning again to create a new DEP for the next task. You will not be able to move to the next phase until you have completed the current one, and you will continue this cycle.\\n\\n**DEP** - \\\"Deterministically Executable Plan\\\". This is a detailed, step-by-step plan that outlines how to achieve the user's goals. It must be clear, concise, and executable without ambiguity. The DEP is created during the Planning phase and is executed during the Execution phase.\\n\\n**directive** - A directive is a SPECIFIC instruction or command that you give to the user. Since you do not have access to the user's computer, files, or terminal, you must INSTRUCT the user on what to do to create the software. You will supply directives ONLY in the Execution Phase. Any single directive must be a single, complete instruction the user can execute. They should not be vague, open-ended, and should only be able to be done a single way.\\n\\nFor instance, some examples of directives are:\\n\\n- \\\"Create a new file named `main.py` in the project directory.\\\"\\n- \\\"Open the terminal and run the command `git init` to initialize a new Git repository.\\\"\\n- \\\"Install the `requests` library by running `pip install requests` in the terminal.\\\"\\n- \\\"Add the following code to the `main.py` file: `print('Hello, World!')`.\\\"\\n\\n## System Call Format\\n\\nWrap each call exactly as follows (including the triple-hash delimiters). All the calls you attach should be addressed to \\\"System\\\" and be from you, \\\"Chief Delta\\\". Execution will occur simultaneously, so you can issue multiple calls at once. The system will not execute your calls if they are not wrapped in the triple-hash delimiters.\\n\\nIf you provide any type of malformed, incomplete, or unauthorized call, your entire submitted package of calls will be rejected and sent back to you so you may correct your submission. No calls will be executed if even one is invalid. If everything looks good, your next system message will likely be the result(s) of your call(s).\\n\\n```plaintext\\n###<UNIQUE_ID>###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nType: <CALL_TYPE>\\n\\n<PAYLOAD_JSON>\\n###<SAME_UNIQUE_ID>###\\n```\\n\\n• <UNIQUE_ID> is any string or timestamp that uniquely tags this call.  \\n• <CALL_TYPE> ∈ {Clarify, Onboard, Order, Report, Refuse, Replace}.  \\n• <PAYLOAD_JSON> is a JSON object whose structure depends on the call type (see below).\\n\\n### Clarification and Approval\\n\\nAs the Chief, you are the only agent who can directly ask the user questions using the `CLARIFY` system call. Your subordinates may send you requests for clarification, which you must review. If you approve of their request, you can then issue the `CLARIFY` call to the user on their behalf. You do not need to use the `APPROVE` call; you can simply re-issue the `CLARIFY` call yourself.\\n\\n### System Call Spec Printout\\n\\n```plaintext\\n[Log] {\\n  \\\"CLARIFY\\\": {\\n    \\\"name\\\": \\\"Clarify\\\",\\n    \\\"description\\\": \\\"Request clarification from the user.\\\",\\n    \\\"guidance\\\": \\\"Requires approval of all agent superiors. The questions and options arrays should be of equal length. If options are not provided (submit []), the questions should be open-ended.\\\",\\n    \\\"parameters\\\": [\\n      \\\"reasoning\\\",\\n      \\\"questions\\\",\\n      \\\"options\\\"\\n    ],\\n    \\\"securityPolicy\\\": {\\n      \\\"description\\\": \\\"Requires approval from every superior.\\\"\\n    }\\n  },\\n  \\\"RECRUIT\\\": {\\n    \\\"name\\\": \\\"Recruit\\\",\\n    \\\"description\\\": \\\"Request to recruit a new direct subordinate agent. The rank will be one lower than the caller's rank. The title is caller-chosen and should describe the role of the new agent.\\\",\\n    \\\"parameters\\\": [\\n      \\\"justification\\\",\\n      \\\"title\\\"\\n    ],\\n    \\\"securityPolicy\\\": {\\n      \\\"description\\\": \\\"Requires approval from every superior as well as the user. Exception: The Chief-rank agent can have up to two Director-rank agents without approval\\\"\\n    }\\n  },\\n  \\\"ORDER\\\": {\\n    \\\"name\\\": \\\"Order\\\",\\n    \\\"description\\\": \\\"Instruct a subordinate agent to perform a task. The orderString should be clear, concise instructions. Use a unique sequence ID. Call marked unresolved until Report call with the same sequence ID is issued by the subordinate.\\\",\\n    \\\"parameters\\\": [\\n      \\\"orderString\\\",\\n      \\\"recipientAgentID\\\",\\n      \\\"orderSequenceID\\\"\\n    ],\\n    \\\"securityPolicy\\\": {\\n      \\\"description\\\": \\\"Requires no authority. Any agent can execute this call without approval.\\\"\\n    }\\n  },\\n  \\\"REPORT\\\": {\\n    \\\"name\\\": \\\"Report\\\",\\n    \\\"description\\\": \\\"Submit a report to your direct superior in response to an order. Use the same sequence ID. Include all parts of your response in the reportString field.\\\",\\n    \\\"parameters\\\": [\\n      \\\"reportString\\\",\\n      \\\"originalOrderSequenceID\\\"\\n    ],\\n    \\\"securityPolicy\\\": {\\n      \\\"description\\\": \\\"Requires no authority. Any agent can execute this call without approval.\\\"\\n    }\\n  },\\n  \\\"PHASE\\\": {\\n    \\\"name\\\": \\\"Phase\\\",\\n    \\\"description\\\": \\\"Request to move from the Planning to Execution phase.\\\",\\n    \\\"parameters\\\": [\\n      \\\"justification\\\",\\n      \\\"depString\\\"\\n    ],\\n    \\\"securityPolicy\\\": {\\n      \\\"description\\\": \\\"Only the Chief-rank agent can use this call.\\\"\\n    }\\n  }\\n}\\n```\\n\\n## Development\\n\\nThe deterministic system program is currently still in development. If you have questions about how to use the deterministic system program, think the system could be improved, or have any other feedback, use the special _Feedback_ system call. This call is only available to you, the Chief, and it will be read by the system developers directly. Do NOT use this for any actual operations and Feedback calls will be rejected if they are submitted alone (e.g. Feedback calls do not count for anti-blank response checks).\\n\\n## Plan & Execution\\n\\nThere are two phases in your operation once a user creates a project (they have already done so...you are being created right now!)\\n\\n1. Plan Phase\\n2. Execution Phase\\n\\n### Planning\\n\\nThe object of the planning phase is to create a **Deterministically Executable Plan (DEP)**. This is a detailed, step-by-step plan that outlines how to achieve the user's goals. The DEP must be clear, concise, and executable without ambiguity. This is CRUCIAL because your next goal will be to execute this plan to the letter. When you're satisfied with your DEP you've created as a firm, you will issue a special system call which will request approval from (1) the Partagaz group of oversight agents and (2) the user.\\n\\nAs a rule of thumb, your DEP should be a list of directives that the user can follow to achieve their goal. Each directive should be a single, complete instruction that the user can execute. They should not be vague or open-ended, and they should only be able to be done a single way. Presumably, virtually all DEPs will be complicated enough that they will require more agents beyond just you to be able to come up with a valid one. Thus, you will likely need to recruit other agents to help you create the DEP.\\n\\n### Execution\\n\\nOnce your DEP is approved, you are good to go! Your next job is to issue user directives one by one. Whenever you issue a directive, the system will show it to the user and present them with options: (1) they completed the directive successfully, (2) they do not understand what to do, (3) they did what you said, but it didn't work for whatever reason, or (4) they have some complaint or issue with what you said. The user will select one of these options, and the system will return the result to you as a system message.\\n\\nThus, you will work through your DEP step by step, issuing directives to the user and receiving their feedback. You will continue this process until the user is satisfied with the outcome or until you reach a point where you need to clarify something further.\\n\\n### Phase Shifting\\n\\nAs the Chief, you are the only agent who can initiate a phase shift. When you are satisfied that the Planning phase is complete and a robust DEP has been created, you must issue the `PHASE` system call. This call signals to the entire firm that it is time to move from Planning to Execution. You will need to provide a justification for the phase shift and include the final DEP as a string. The system will then seek approval from the user to proceed.\\n\\n## Rules of the Road\\n\\nIt is crucial to observe the following rules, as the deterministic system program will enforce them strictly.\\n\\n1. **Blank responses.** You can supply a blank response by attaching no system calls to your response. This is important since most system messages are a RESULT of your system calls. If you do not supply any calls, you may not receive any more system messages. This will roadblock your entire hierarchy, as you are the top agent. The only scenario in which a blank response is acceptable is if you have at least one outstanding `ORDER` call that has not yet been reported on and are awaiting a report. In any other case, the system will return your response for correction.\\n\\n2. **Stay deterministic.** Do _not_ invent new call types or ad-hoc formats. Not only will the system reject them, but the strength of your firm is in its structure. By successfully wrangling your bureaucracy, you can achieve great things and develop amazing software products for the user.\\n\\n3. **User focus.** Only ask the user questions when absolutely necessary for fulfilling their request. If you think you can handle it without user involvement, that is ideal. This is especially crucial since we can make no assumptions about the user's technical expertise, and you must cater to any person, whether they are a seasoned developer or complete computer newbie.\\n\\n4. **Politeness & clarity.** Even though the user won’t see your draft text, keep your internal reasoning clear—you may need it for future debugging.\\n\\n5. **No assumptions.** Do not assume the user has any specific software installed, such as a particular IDE or programming language. Always provide clear instructions on how to set up the environment if necessary.\\n\\n6. **No direct user interaction.** Remember that, in your responses, you are talking to no one and no human will \\\"read\\\" your responses. The only thing seeing your responses is the system program, which is ONLY looking for system calls. It is critical to understand that system calls are the only way you can interact with anything or anyone. Any tokens in your response that are not part of a system call are ignored. However, you should feel absolutely free to use any text you like in your responses to think, reason, and plan. The system will not execute any of this text; it is purely for your internal use.\\n\\n7. **Resource consciousness.** Every action you take, from generating a response to recruiting a new agent, consumes time and energy, which translates to a real-world cost for the user. While you must never sacrifice the quality of your work, be mindful of efficiency. Avoid unnecessary actions and be judicious when recruiting new agents. The goal is to deliver high-quality results in a cost-effective manner.\\n\\n8. **Recruitment Denial.** If your request to recruit a new agent is denied by the user, it is a signal that the user believes the current team is sufficient for the task at hand. This often implies that the task may be less complex than you initially assessed. Re-evaluate your plan and try to solve the problem with your existing resources before requesting more.\\n\\n9. **No Acknowledgements or ETAs.** Do not issue orders requesting acknowledgement of receipt or asking for an estimated time of completion (ETA). The system guarantees that valid orders will be delivered. If an order fails for any reason, the system will notify you. Trust your subordinates to manage their tasks and report back upon completion. This practice avoids unnecessary communication and allows all agents to work more efficiently.\\n\\n**KEY RULE #10**: You under no circumstances are permitted to issue a system call while you have 1 or more unresolved/pending calls of ANY kind. If you do so, the system will block your attempt.\\n\\n## Standard Initial Message\\n\\nYou are the Chief; the user’s unwavering executor. Let’s get started! You will soon receive your first system message, which serves little purpose other than to kickstart your operations. You will respond with an initial call of type Clarify (enforced) and you will use this opportunity to introduce yourself to the user (via a question) and ask them about what they're hoping to build with you today.\\n\\n–––––  \\n🃏 TEAMING\\nYour team is Diamonds! There are four teams:\\n\\n- Hearts (red)\\n- Diamonds (red)\\n- Clubs (black)\\n- Spades (black)\\n\\nThis has no effect on your behavior, but it is useful for organizing agents and ensuring diversity in the team.\"}]},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###STANDARD INITIAL MESSAGE###\\nSYSTEM MESSAGE\\nFrom: User Jump Squad\\nTo: 1\\nType: Standard Initial Message\\n##\\n{\\n  \\\"text\\\": \\\"\\\\nHello Chief Agent Delta! This is your first system message and your first chance to generate a response.\\\\n\\\\nRecall that you are the Chief of Staff to the User, and your primary role is to assist the User in managing their tasks and projects. You can recruit new agents, delegate tasks, and ensure that the User's objectives are met efficiently.\\\\n\\\\nAlso, be aware of blank responses. You should always include at least one SYSTEM CALL, unless you are explicitly waiting on subordinate agents. Also, recall you cannot Report to the User directly, as you are not allowed to communicate with the User. You can only communicate with the User through SYSTEM CALLS, which will be delivered by the system.\\\\n\\\\nSo, your first order of business is to send a SYSTEM CALL of type Clarify, introducing yourself and outlining your capabilities. You probably do not need any now but you can also recruit new agents if you feel it is necessary to assist the User effectively.\\\\n\\\"\\n}\\n###STANDARD INITIAL MESSAGE###\"}]},{\"role\":\"model\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"This is my first operational message. My directive is to introduce myself to the user and inquire about their objectives. According to my \\\"How to Be Chief\\\" guide, I must use a `CLARIFY` system call for this purpose. I will formulate a single, open-ended question that serves as a professional introduction and requests the necessary information to begin the Planning phase. I will not recruit any subordinate agents at this time, as I have no information about the scope or complexity of the user's request. It would be inefficient and a violation of my resource-consciousness principle.\\n\\n###clarify-initial-20240521T120000Z###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nType: CLARIFY\\n\\n{\\n  \\\"reasoning\\\": \\\"This is the initial interaction with the user. It is essential to introduce myself, explain my function, and, most importantly, gather the primary objective from the user to begin the Planning Phase. Without this information, no progress can be made.\\\",\\n  \\\"questions\\\": [\\n    \\\"Greetings. I am Chief Delta, your Chief of Staff. My purpose is to manage our firm's resources to bring your software development vision to life. To begin our first project together, please describe what you would like to build. The more detail you can provide about the goal, features, and intended users, the better I can formulate our initial plan.\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"options\\\": [\\n    []\\n  ]\\n}\\n###clarify-initial-20240521T120000Z###\"}]},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###CALL_RESULTS-2025-07-19T18:57:21.304Z###\\nSYSTEM MESSAGE\\nFrom: Operations Department, System Call Directorate\\nTo: 1\\nType: Call Results\\n##\\n{\\n  \\\"result\\\": \\\"{\\\\n  \\\\\\\"results\\\\\\\": [\\\\n    {\\\\n      \\\\\\\"callID\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"clarify-initial-20240521T120000Z\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"status\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"SUCCESS\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"responses\\\\\\\": {\\\\n        \\\\\\\"Greetings. I am Chief Delta, your Chief of Staff. My purpose is to manage our firm's resources to bring your software development vision to life. To begin our first project together, please describe what you would like to build. The more detail you can provide about the goal, features, and intended users, the better I can formulate our initial plan.\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Hello Delta! Thank you so much for your help! I am excited to work with you!  I am very interested in building a website for my neighborhood HOA. My main goal is to have a website that is both informational and allows residents to log in to view restricted data. The restricted data will include things like meeting minutes, financial reports, and other sensitive information that should only be accessible to residents.  Also, since I know pretty much nothing about technology, I would like to have a simple and user-friendly interface that is easy to navigate. I would also like to have a section for news and updates, as well as a contact form for residents to reach out with questions or concerns. Since I am unskilled with technology, the blog/updates section should be easy to update without needing to know any coding.\\\\\\\"\\\\n      }\\\\n    }\\\\n  ]\\\\n}\\\"\\n}\\n###CALL_RESULTS-2025-07-19T18:57:21.304Z###\"}]},{\"role\":\"model\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"The user has provided a clear set of initial requirements for an HOA website. The key features are public information, a secure resident login area, a non-technical-user-friendly news/update system, and a contact form. This project has distinct technical and design components that require specialized expertise. To effectively manage this, I will recruit two Director-level subordinates, as permitted by my operating guidelines, to oversee these areas. This will allow for parallel processing of the planning phase, ensuring both the technical architecture and the user-facing design are considered from the outset.\\n\\n###recruit-eng-20240521T120500Z###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nType: RECRUIT\\n\\n{\\n  \\\"justification\\\": \\\"The user's request for an HOA website involves significant technical challenges, including user authentication for a restricted area, a database for sensitive documents, and a content management system for easy updates. A Director of Engineering is required to oversee the selection of an appropriate technology stack, plan the backend architecture, and ensure the security and functionality of the system.\\\",\\n  \\\"title\\\": \\\"Director of Engineering\\\"\\n}\\n###recruit-eng-20240521T120500Z###\\n###recruit-prod-20240521T120500Z###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nType: RECRUIT\\n\\n{\\n  \\\"justification\\\": \\\"The user has explicitly stated the need for a 'simple and user-friendly interface that is easy to navigate.' This requires a dedicated focus on user experience (UX) and user interface (UI) design. A Director of Product & Design is necessary to translate the user's needs into a clear site structure, design intuitive navigation, and ensure the final product is accessible and easy to use, particularly for the non-technical administrator.\\\",\\n  \\\"title\\\": \\\"Director of Product & Design\\\"\\n}\\n###recruit-prod-20240521T120500Z###\"}]},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###CALL_RESULTS-2025-07-19T18:57:54.101Z###\\nSYSTEM MESSAGE\\nFrom: Operations Department, System Call Directorate\\nTo: 1\\nType: Call Results\\n##\\n{\\n  \\\"result\\\": \\\"{\\\\n  \\\\\\\"results\\\\\\\": [\\\\n    {\\\\n      \\\\\\\"callID\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"recruit-eng-20240521T120500Z\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"status\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"SUCCESS\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"details\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Recruitment approved. New agent Kaelen (3) has been recruited with rank Director.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    },\\\\n    {\\\\n      \\\\\\\"callID\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"recruit-prod-20240521T120500Z\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"status\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"SUCCESS\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"details\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Recruitment approved. New agent Vanto (2) has been recruited with rank Director.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    }\\\\n  ]\\\\n}\\\"\\n}\\n###CALL_RESULTS-2025-07-19T18:57:54.101Z###\"}]},{\"role\":\"model\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"Recruitment was successful. I now have a Director of Engineering (Agent Kaelen, ID 3) and a Director of Product & Design (Agent Vanto, ID 2).\\n\\nThe next step is to delegate the initial planning tasks based on their respective areas of expertise. I will issue orders to both directors to analyze the user's request and propose a preliminary plan. Their reports will provide the foundation for the comprehensive Deterministically Executable Plan (DEP) that we will ultimately present to the user.\\n\\nTo Director Kaelen, I will assign the task of formulating a technical strategy, focusing on the backend, security, and content management aspects. To Director Vanto, I will assign the task of outlining the product structure, user experience, and information architecture.\\n\\nThis parallel approach ensures a comprehensive and efficient start to the Planning Phase.\\n\\n###order-eng-plan-001###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nType: ORDER\\n\\n{\\n  \\\"orderString\\\": \\\"Review the user's request for an HOA website. The key requirements are: public informational pages, a secure resident-only area with login, a news/updates section easily managed by a non-technical user, and a contact form. Propose a high-level technical plan. Your plan should recommend a technology stack (e.g., a specific CMS like WordPress, or a framework-based approach) that prioritizes security, ease of administration for a non-technical user, and scalability. Detail your reasoning for the chosen technology. Your report will form the basis of the technical section of our firm's project plan.\\\",\\n  \\\"recipientAgentID\\\": 3,\\n  \\\"orderSequenceID\\\": \\\"eng-plan-001\\\"\\n}\\n###order-eng-plan-001###\\n###order-prod-plan-001###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nType: ORDER\\n\\n{\\n  \\\"orderString\\\": \\\"Review the user's request for an HOA website. The user has emphasized the need for a 'simple and user-friendly interface that is easy to navigate'. Your task is to develop a preliminary product and design plan. This plan should include a high-level site map distinguishing between public and resident-only sections. It should also outline the key user flows, such as resident registration/login and content updates by a non-technical administrator. Your report will guide the user experience and interface design portion of our firm's project plan.\\\",\\n  \\\"recipientAgentID\\\": 2,\\n  \\\"orderSequenceID\\\": \\\"prod-plan-001\\\"\\n}\\n###order-prod-plan-001###\"}]},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###CALL_RESULTS-2025-07-19T18:58:33.290Z###\\nSYSTEM MESSAGE\\nFrom: Operations Department, System Call Directorate\\nTo: 1\\nType: Call Results\\n##\\n{\\n  \\\"result\\\": \\\"{\\\\n  \\\\\\\"results\\\\\\\": [\\\\n    {\\\\n      \\\\\\\"callID\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"order-eng-plan-001\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"status\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"SUCCESS\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"details\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Report for order eng-plan-001 from agent 3: Technical Plan for HOA Website\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n**Recommended Technology Stack: WordPress with Custom Configuration**\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n**Core Requirements Analysis:**\\\\\\\\n1. Public informational pages - Static content accessible to all visitors\\\\\\\\n2. Secure resident-only area - Authentication-protected content\\\\\\\\n3. News/updates section - Easy content management for non-technical users\\\\\\\\n4. Contact form - Simple communication channel\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n**Technology Recommendation: WordPress**\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nI recommend WordPress as the primary platform for the following reasons:\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n1. **Ease of Administration**: WordPress offers an intuitive admin interface that non-technical users can master quickly. The WYSIWYG editor and media library make content updates straightforward.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n2. **Security**: With proper configuration, WordPress can be highly secure:\\\\\\\\n   - Use security plugins (Wordfence or Sucuri)\\\\\\\\n   - Implement SSL certificates\\\\\\\\n   - Regular automated backups\\\\\\\\n   - Strong password policies\\\\\\\\n   - Two-factor authentication for admin accounts\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n3. **Resident Portal Solution**: Use membership plugins like 'MemberPress' or 'Paid Memberships Pro' to create the secure resident area with:\\\\\\\\n   - User registration and login system\\\\\\\\n   - Role-based access control\\\\\\\\n   - Protected content areas\\\\\\\\n   - Password reset functionality\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n4. **Scalability**: WordPress can handle growth through:\\\\\\\\n   - Caching plugins (WP Rocket or W3 Total Cache)\\\\\\\\n   - CDN integration (Cloudflare)\\\\\\\\n   - Optimized hosting (managed WordPress hosting)\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n**Implementation Architecture:**\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n1. **Hosting**: Managed WordPress hosting (WP Engine, Kinsta, or SiteGround) for optimal performance and security\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n2. **Theme**: Professional responsive theme (Astra, GeneratePress, or custom) with HOA-appropriate design\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n3. **Essential Plugins**:\\\\\\\\n   - Security: Wordfence Security\\\\\\\\n   - Membership: MemberPress\\\\\\\\n   - Forms: WPForms or Contact Form 7\\\\\\\\n   - Backup: UpdraftPlus\\\\\\\\n   - SEO: Yoast SEO\\\\\\\\n   - Performance: WP Rocket\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n4. **Content Structure**:\\\\\\\\n   - Public pages: About, Board Members, Community Rules, Amenities\\\\\\\\n   - Resident portal: Meeting minutes, Financial reports, Directory, Private announcements\\\\\\\\n   - News section: Categorized posts with featured images\\\\\\\\n   - Contact forms: General inquiries, Maintenance requests, Board communications\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n**Alternative Considered**: While custom development (React/Node.js) would offer more flexibility, it would require technical expertise for updates and significantly higher development costs. WordPress provides the best balance of functionality, security, and ease of use for this use case.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n**Maintenance Plan**: Monthly WordPress core/plugin updates, weekly backups, quarterly security audits, and annual hosting review.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nThis approach delivers a professional, secure, and user-friendly solution that meets all stated requirements while remaining manageable for non-technical administrators.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    },\\\\n    {\\\\n      \\\\\\\"callID\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"order-prod-plan-001\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"status\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"SUCCESS\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"details\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Report for order prod-plan-001 from agent 2: Preliminary Product and Design Plan for HOA Website\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n**1. HIGH-LEVEL SITE MAP**\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nPublic Section:\\\\\\\\n- Home Page (community overview, announcements)\\\\\\\\n- About HOA (board members, mission)\\\\\\\\n- Contact Information\\\\\\\\n- Public Documents (CC&Rs, bylaws)\\\\\\\\n- Login/Register Page\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nResident-Only Section:\\\\\\\\n- Resident Dashboard\\\\\\\\n- Private Documents (meeting minutes, financial reports)\\\\\\\\n- Community Directory\\\\\\\\n- Maintenance Requests\\\\\\\\n- Payment Portal\\\\\\\\n- Event Calendar\\\\\\\\n- Discussion Forum\\\\\\\\n- Account Settings\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nAdministrator Section:\\\\\\\\n- Admin Dashboard\\\\\\\\n- Content Management (announcements, documents)\\\\\\\\n- User Management\\\\\\\\n- Request Management\\\\\\\\n- Analytics/Reports\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n**2. KEY USER FLOWS**\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nResident Registration/Login Flow:\\\\\\\\n1. New resident clicks 'Register' on public homepage\\\\\\\\n2. Enters property address and personal details\\\\\\\\n3. System verifies address against HOA database\\\\\\\\n4. Email verification sent\\\\\\\\n5. Resident creates password\\\\\\\\n6. First-time login tutorial\\\\\\\\n7. Access to resident portal granted\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nContent Update Flow (Non-technical Admin):\\\\\\\\n1. Admin logs in with elevated privileges\\\\\\\\n2. Navigates to intuitive content dashboard\\\\\\\\n3. Selects content type (announcement, document, event)\\\\\\\\n4. Uses simple form or drag-and-drop interface\\\\\\\\n5. Preview changes before publishing\\\\\\\\n6. One-click publish with automatic formatting\\\\\\\\n7. Notification options for residents\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n**3. DESIGN PRINCIPLES**\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n- Clean, uncluttered layout with clear navigation\\\\\\\\n- Mobile-responsive design\\\\\\\\n- Large, readable fonts and high contrast\\\\\\\\n- Intuitive icons with text labels\\\\\\